1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:09,636
[Dive Into You]

2
00:00:10,136 --> 00:00:14,446
[This is a fictional story. All characters
and events bear no relation to reality]

3
00:00:20,899 --> 00:00:22,868
[2010 Haesol City
Superintendent's Cup Judo Tournament]

4
00:00:25,011 --> 00:00:26,788
[Sharp skills, strong mind! Go Haesol
Judo Team! Haesol's pride is on the line!]

5
00:00:26,812 --> 00:00:31,217
[Finals]
[Haesol High Jung Woo Jae : Yoon Ha Ru]

6
00:00:32,174 --> 00:00:34,466
<i>What is this? Is it a dream?</i>

7
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:37,577
<i>2010?</i>

8
00:00:37,577 --> 00:00:38,779
Everyone in the center, please.

9
00:00:38,779 --> 00:00:41,315
<i>What? Is he talking to me?</i>

10
00:00:41,315 --> 00:00:43,268
Player Yoon Ha Ru, what are you doing?

11
00:00:43,268 --> 00:00:44,876
Come on, onto the mat, please.

12
00:00:44,876 --> 00:00:46,560
<i>Why is he telling me that?</i>

13
00:00:47,150 --> 00:00:49,663
<i>What is this?</i>

14
00:00:50,739 --> 00:00:52,439
<i>Woo Jae!</i>

15
00:00:54,027 --> 00:00:55,727
<i>Jung Woo Jae!</i>

16
00:01:00,366 --> 00:01:01,834
<i>What is this?</i>

17
00:01:01,834 --> 00:01:03,534
<i>Where am I?</i>

18
00:01:04,162 --> 00:01:05,862
<i>Mom? Dad?</i>

19
00:01:07,459 --> 00:01:09,159
<i>Jung Woo Jae?</i>

20
00:01:11,922 --> 00:01:13,622
Woo Jae!

21
00:01:18,026 --> 00:01:20,179
- What the...
- What is he doing?

22
00:01:20,179 --> 00:01:21,847
- What?
- Yoon Ha Ru?

23
00:01:21,847 --> 00:01:23,633
- What's going on?
- Ha Ru?

24
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:25,457
He's just nervous. That must be it.

25
00:01:25,457 --> 00:01:28,197
- It's just nerves.
- Surely, yeah.

26
00:01:30,474 --> 00:01:32,174
Hey!

27
00:01:34,278 --> 00:01:35,764
Start!

28
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:46,060
Woo Jae, full point!

29
00:01:56,112 --> 00:01:57,713
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

30
00:01:57,713 --> 00:01:59,413
You okay?

31
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:09,104
Wait, are you crying?

32
00:02:09,104 --> 00:02:10,491
Huh?

33
00:02:13,522 --> 00:02:14,606
No way.

34
00:02:14,606 --> 00:02:17,671
Are you crying because you lost to me?

35
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:21,620
What?

36
00:02:22,534 --> 00:02:25,604
What am I... doing over there?

37
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,860
What am I doing over there?

38
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:41,696
Where do you think you're touching,
you bastard?

39
00:02:41,696 --> 00:02:43,396
What the heck!

40
00:03:02,857 --> 00:03:04,501
- Honey, come here, look!
- Honey...

41
00:03:04,501 --> 00:03:05,872
Ha Na is awake!

42
00:03:05,872 --> 00:03:07,225
Ha Ru, too!

43
00:03:07,225 --> 00:03:09,391
Ha Ru, Ha Ru!

44
00:03:09,391 --> 00:03:11,003
Oh, thank goodness! Thank goodness!

45
00:03:11,003 --> 00:03:13,905
Doctor! They're awake!

46
00:03:13,905 --> 00:03:15,881
I'll go get someone, honey.

47
00:03:15,881 --> 00:03:17,118
Nurse!

48
00:03:17,118 --> 00:03:18,372
Ha Ru.

49
00:03:18,372 --> 00:03:19,620
Ha Na.

50
00:03:19,620 --> 00:03:21,172
Can you see me? It's Mom.

51
00:03:21,172 --> 00:03:23,375
Mom...

52
00:03:23,375 --> 00:03:25,752
Thank goodness, oh, good heavens!

53
00:03:25,752 --> 00:03:27,308
Everything's going to be fine
now that you're awake!

54
00:03:27,308 --> 00:03:29,541
- Oh, my sweet children!
- Mom...

55
00:03:31,101 --> 00:03:33,325
Yes, darling? What is it?

56
00:03:33,325 --> 00:03:35,025
Where is Woo Jae?

57
00:03:35,645 --> 00:03:39,712
He was... with me just now.

58
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:44,852
Did you have a dream about him?

59
00:03:44,852 --> 00:03:46,058
A dream?

60
00:03:46,058 --> 00:03:47,340
Ha Na.

61
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,899
I'm sure Woo Jae is in a better place now.

62
00:03:49,899 --> 00:03:52,311
He was a good boy.

63
00:03:53,349 --> 00:03:55,049
That was a dream?

64
00:03:58,812 --> 00:04:00,752
That was just a dream?

65
00:04:02,201 --> 00:04:03,798
What's taking your dad so long anyway?

66
00:04:03,798 --> 00:04:05,958
He's supposed to be back with a doctor by now.

67
00:04:15,823 --> 00:04:17,523
I saw him, too.

68
00:04:18,442 --> 00:04:20,142
Jung Woo Jae.

69
00:04:27,393 --> 00:04:31,217
Do twins have matching dreams?
Is that even a thing?

70
00:04:32,414 --> 00:04:34,854
What a messed-up dream.

71
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:38,377
The dream...

72
00:04:39,572 --> 00:04:41,813
It was so vivid.

73
00:04:43,416 --> 00:04:46,411
I could hear him breathe up close.

74
00:04:47,952 --> 00:04:50,349
I wish it lasted longer.

75
00:04:51,481 --> 00:04:54,379
We could've had more time together.

76
00:04:55,823 --> 00:04:58,116
I wish I never woke up.

77
00:05:00,317 --> 00:05:01,887
Huh?

78
00:05:04,723 --> 00:05:06,144
What?

79
00:05:10,498 --> 00:05:12,015
Hey.

80
00:05:12,015 --> 00:05:13,290
Yoon Ha Na.

81
00:05:13,290 --> 00:05:14,836
What?

82
00:05:14,836 --> 00:05:16,536
This is...

83
00:05:18,232 --> 00:05:19,869
What is this?

84
00:05:19,869 --> 00:05:21,952
What are you talking about?

85
00:05:21,952 --> 00:05:23,083
It changed.

86
00:05:23,083 --> 00:05:24,783
What did?

87
00:05:27,056 --> 00:05:28,742
The medal!

88
00:05:28,742 --> 00:05:30,366
I got the gold medal that day, right?

89
00:05:30,366 --> 00:05:32,799
Now it's silver!

90
00:05:41,086 --> 00:05:42,554
Huh?

91
00:05:56,026 --> 00:05:58,276
What in the...

92
00:06:00,913 --> 00:06:04,270
Did I... really do that?

93
00:06:04,270 --> 00:06:07,259
Wait, that's...

94
00:06:07,259 --> 00:06:09,301
That's me!

95
00:06:10,309 --> 00:06:11,700
Huh?

96
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,400
Rewind it one more time.

97
00:06:20,122 --> 00:06:22,053
So, what you're saying is...

98
00:06:22,053 --> 00:06:25,373
that that wasn't actually a dream?

99
00:06:25,373 --> 00:06:27,706
If it had been,
how would the medal have changed?

100
00:06:27,706 --> 00:06:29,379
And the video changed as well.

101
00:06:29,379 --> 00:06:31,539
It mysteriously disappeared, too, right?

102
00:06:31,539 --> 00:06:33,680
It's suspicious, no?

103
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:35,827
Maybe we're still dreaming?

104
00:06:39,315 --> 00:06:40,433
I guess not.

105
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:42,840
It absolutely wasn't a dream.

106
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:44,797
How does that make any sense?

107
00:06:44,797 --> 00:06:46,497
It makes no sense...

108
00:06:48,145 --> 00:06:50,567
- Or does it?
- Well, what if...

109
00:06:50,567 --> 00:06:52,061
it does make sense?

110
00:06:52,854 --> 00:06:53,866
Huh?

111
00:06:53,866 --> 00:06:55,666
If we can go back in time,

112
00:06:55,666 --> 00:06:58,866
and change the color of the medal...

113
00:06:58,866 --> 00:06:59,955
Then...

114
00:06:59,955 --> 00:07:01,372
Woo Jae.

115
00:07:01,372 --> 00:07:03,735
Maybe we could do the same with him.

116
00:07:11,142 --> 00:07:14,100
Wait, why isn't it working?

117
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,800
How do I do this?

118
00:07:16,726 --> 00:07:18,426
Give it here.

119
00:07:20,848 --> 00:07:23,923
Have you lost it?
That thing's already old as bones!

120
00:07:25,061 --> 00:07:26,558
Sorry.

121
00:07:28,061 --> 00:07:30,126
Let's do a recap.

122
00:07:30,126 --> 00:07:31,630
Okay.

123
00:07:32,788 --> 00:07:35,075
We were on our way home...

124
00:07:35,075 --> 00:07:37,888
When a truck hurtled our way.

125
00:07:37,888 --> 00:07:40,002
Then the camcorder started
playing back a video on its own.

126
00:07:40,002 --> 00:07:41,689
That's everything I can recall.

127
00:07:41,689 --> 00:07:43,778
Do you remember anything else?

128
00:07:43,778 --> 00:07:45,899
I've got nothing after the truck.

129
00:07:45,899 --> 00:07:47,754
I don't know what you want me to say.

130
00:07:52,133 --> 00:07:53,833
And...

131
00:07:54,500 --> 00:07:56,137
When I came to,

132
00:07:56,137 --> 00:07:58,260
I was recording Woo Jae and me
with the camcorder.

133
00:07:58,260 --> 00:08:00,000
Well, not me, you.

134
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,553
Anyway...

135
00:08:01,553 --> 00:08:03,553
I was recording. That's the point.

136
00:08:03,553 --> 00:08:07,199
Then, I saw the match end in,
what, 3 seconds with a full point.

137
00:08:07,199 --> 00:08:09,386
There were tears, Woo Jae was confused...

138
00:08:09,386 --> 00:08:12,205
Well, I thought it was all a dream.
But something was clearly off.

139
00:08:12,205 --> 00:08:14,921
So I was feeling myself up a little,

140
00:08:15,589 --> 00:08:17,286
and felt something weird on my chest...

141
00:08:17,286 --> 00:08:18,920
That's enough, I get it.

142
00:08:18,920 --> 00:08:21,277
I saw it with my own eyes.

143
00:08:21,277 --> 00:08:22,719
I was shocked, too, you know.

144
00:08:22,719 --> 00:08:25,593
That's why I dropped the camcorder,
and that was that.

145
00:08:26,219 --> 00:08:29,574
And so we returned to the present, right?

146
00:08:36,266 --> 00:08:38,076
- Ready?
- Yeah.

147
00:08:38,076 --> 00:08:39,776
Here goes.

148
00:08:40,365 --> 00:08:42,624
One, two, three.

149
00:08:52,999 --> 00:08:55,608
Dang it. It's not working.

150
00:08:57,528 --> 00:08:59,228
Ow, my legs.

151
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:02,667
I guess your legs are too short to hurt, huh?

152
00:09:28,652 --> 00:09:30,536
It's not working.

153
00:09:30,536 --> 00:09:31,740
Dive in.

154
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:33,440
Dive in?

155
00:09:34,372 --> 00:09:36,072
Okay. Sure...

156
00:09:44,365 --> 00:09:46,711
No, hold on a little longer!

157
00:09:54,528 --> 00:09:56,661
I almost drowned!

158
00:10:22,555 --> 00:10:25,546
It looks... pretty deep, huh?

159
00:10:25,546 --> 00:10:27,633
Well...

160
00:10:27,633 --> 00:10:30,061
We need to jump at the same time.

161
00:10:30,061 --> 00:10:31,839
Of course.

162
00:10:31,839 --> 00:10:34,148
At the same time. Yeah, I know.

163
00:10:34,148 --> 00:10:36,386
Together, yeah, obviously.

164
00:10:36,386 --> 00:10:38,590
- Are you scared?
- Of course I...

165
00:10:43,744 --> 00:10:45,239
Scared?

166
00:10:45,239 --> 00:10:47,972
Wow, really, Yoon Ha Na?

167
00:10:47,972 --> 00:10:49,349
This is Yoon Ha Ru we're talking about.

168
00:10:49,349 --> 00:10:52,293
Your big brother doesn't feel fear at all.

169
00:10:52,293 --> 00:10:55,274
Honestly, I don't know
what that word even means.

170
00:10:56,348 --> 00:10:58,246
Your left leg has been shaking non-stop
for the last few minutes.

171
00:10:58,246 --> 00:10:59,605
Huh?

172
00:11:03,678 --> 00:11:05,126
I'm not shaking.

173
00:11:05,126 --> 00:11:06,623
I'm just getting the engine started.

174
00:11:06,623 --> 00:11:08,121
What's it to you?

175
00:11:10,953 --> 00:11:14,142
Why is the water... so pitch black?

176
00:11:14,142 --> 00:11:17,422
It's making me imagine things
lurking underneath the surface.

177
00:11:19,679 --> 00:11:23,919
You sure have the ample imagination
of the actress that you are.

178
00:11:23,919 --> 00:11:25,658
This is an indoor pool.

179
00:11:25,658 --> 00:11:27,344
There's nothing in the water.

180
00:11:27,344 --> 00:11:28,815
And I have to tell you...

181
00:11:28,815 --> 00:11:30,359
I'm a very good swimmer.

182
00:11:30,359 --> 00:11:33,812
You know that I was in the
children's swimming team.

183
00:11:37,101 --> 00:11:39,397
Actually, I'm scared, too.

184
00:11:40,731 --> 00:11:42,842
But...

185
00:11:42,842 --> 00:11:45,620
As long as there's even a slim chance of hope,

186
00:11:46,279 --> 00:11:48,220
I'd do anything.

187
00:11:52,225 --> 00:11:54,222
Me too.

188
00:11:54,222 --> 00:11:56,234
Because it's Jung Woo Jae.

189
00:11:57,502 --> 00:11:58,925
Yeah.

190
00:11:58,925 --> 00:12:00,865
Because it's Jung Woo Jae.

191
00:12:31,888 --> 00:12:34,629
<i>My heart is racing.</i>

192
00:12:35,446 --> 00:12:37,496
Hold your breath, Yoon Ha Ru.

193
00:12:37,496 --> 00:12:38,957
Got it.

194
00:12:40,853 --> 00:12:44,009
<i>Out of fear, or from excitement...</i>

195
00:12:44,009 --> 00:12:45,830
<i>I'll never know for sure.</i>

196
00:12:49,722 --> 00:12:51,903
<i>But I don't hesitate for even a moment...</i>

197
00:12:52,915 --> 00:12:54,997
<i>as I dive into the emptiness below.</i>

198
00:13:13,435 --> 00:13:15,041
<i>Into Jung Woo Jae.</i>

199
00:13:18,482 --> 00:13:20,182
<i>Into you.</i>

200
00:13:32,496 --> 00:13:33,952
<i>What's this?</i>

201
00:13:36,456 --> 00:13:38,156
<i>What's going on?</i>

202
00:13:39,708 --> 00:13:41,408
<i>What is happening?</i>

203
00:13:43,314 --> 00:13:45,545
What the...

204
00:13:45,545 --> 00:13:46,722
What?

205
00:13:46,722 --> 00:13:48,268
What is that?

206
00:13:51,705 --> 00:13:53,405
That scared me!

207
00:13:54,435 --> 00:13:56,168
Darn it, Yoon Ha Na!

208
00:13:59,168 --> 00:14:01,935
You! What's up with this face?
In the middle of the night, no less!

209
00:14:01,935 --> 00:14:04,089
I thought I crossed the Styx or something!

210
00:14:04,089 --> 00:14:05,670
Yoon Ha Ru?

211
00:14:06,572 --> 00:14:12,333
Ah, I was preparing for
an audition on this day.

212
00:14:13,007 --> 00:14:14,482
The makeup looks pretty good.

213
00:14:14,482 --> 00:14:16,182
It's captured the vibe well.

214
00:14:17,265 --> 00:14:19,132
Oh, my heart.

215
00:14:24,797 --> 00:14:27,225
It's 2010.

216
00:14:27,225 --> 00:14:29,060
Are you serious?

217
00:14:32,608 --> 00:14:34,152
This is the one, right?

218
00:14:34,152 --> 00:14:35,852
The time machine?

219
00:14:40,678 --> 00:14:43,158
December 31st, 2010...

220
00:14:43,158 --> 00:14:44,533
That's the date of the second video.

221
00:14:44,533 --> 00:14:46,518
We made it.

222
00:14:47,696 --> 00:14:50,525
We actually traveled back in time?

223
00:14:50,525 --> 00:14:52,152
Yes.

224
00:14:52,152 --> 00:14:54,219
Wait, what?

225
00:14:54,219 --> 00:14:56,506
Huh? What's wrong?

226
00:14:56,506 --> 00:14:58,206
We're in some deep trouble, then.

227
00:14:58,893 --> 00:15:01,192
Real deep trouble.

228
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:02,892
Why? What is it?

229
00:15:06,681 --> 00:15:09,120
I am so gosh darn charmingly handsome.

230
00:15:10,499 --> 00:15:12,135
Do you actually want to cross the Styx?

231
00:15:12,135 --> 00:15:13,846
This skin...

232
00:15:13,846 --> 00:15:15,899
No amount of product or treatment
could ever recreate this.

233
00:15:15,899 --> 00:15:17,864
This is the real thing, real baby-soft skin!

234
00:15:17,864 --> 00:15:19,427
Get off me!

235
00:15:19,427 --> 00:15:21,960
You are one unhinged bastard!

236
00:15:23,642 --> 00:15:26,058
I should be the one on the big screen, not you.

237
00:15:27,659 --> 00:15:29,183
It's Woo Jae!

238
00:15:29,183 --> 00:15:31,018
What?

239
00:15:31,018 --> 00:15:33,519
<i>Meet me at the place at 11:20.</i>

240
00:15:36,104 --> 00:15:38,765
Wait for me!

241
00:15:38,765 --> 00:15:42,021
Ugh, your hair is annoying!
I should just chop it off!

242
00:15:49,786 --> 00:15:51,081
You can cut it if you dare.

243
00:15:51,081 --> 00:15:53,350
I'll fill up on grilled pork belly
right before the national team trial,

244
00:15:53,350 --> 00:15:55,667
so that you never pass the
competition in the first place.

245
00:15:55,667 --> 00:15:58,121
You'll never even bear the Taegeuk symbol.

246
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:01,587
Where are you even going?

247
00:16:01,587 --> 00:16:02,730
I don't know.

248
00:16:02,730 --> 00:16:04,522
It's too late to just walk off
without a clear destination!

249
00:16:04,522 --> 00:16:07,393
Well, Woo Jae wants to meet up!
I can't just sit around doing nothing!

250
00:16:08,159 --> 00:16:10,372
December 31st...

251
00:16:10,372 --> 00:16:12,673
What were we doing that day?

252
00:16:12,673 --> 00:16:14,035
Why did we meet up?

253
00:16:14,035 --> 00:16:15,190
December... 31st...

254
00:16:15,190 --> 00:16:17,682
It's the last day of the year, so...

255
00:16:18,828 --> 00:16:20,528
- The beach!
- The beach!

256
00:16:21,326 --> 00:16:23,462
Wait, help me tie my hair up first!

257
00:16:23,462 --> 00:16:25,266
I'm seriously going to cut it off!

258
00:16:25,266 --> 00:16:26,966
I'm not bluffing!

259
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:33,527
He's not here.

260
00:16:33,527 --> 00:16:34,884
Is this not the place?

261
00:16:34,884 --> 00:16:36,735
No, it is.

262
00:16:36,735 --> 00:16:38,645
This is the place, but...

263
00:16:40,109 --> 00:16:41,851
It's past 11:50 now.

264
00:16:41,851 --> 00:16:43,849
So why isn't he here?

265
00:16:44,777 --> 00:16:46,908
Where are you, Jung Woo Jae?

266
00:16:46,908 --> 00:16:48,840
Wait, I'll call him.

267
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,579
Hey, Ha Na.

268
00:17:13,330 --> 00:17:15,030
<i>Jung Woo Jae...</i>

269
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:23,190
Jung Woo Jae, you bastard!

270
00:17:23,190 --> 00:17:26,262
Jung Woo Jae, where the heck were you?

271
00:17:26,262 --> 00:17:28,939
Where were you? Tell me!

272
00:17:28,939 --> 00:17:31,252
We were supposed to meet
in front of the campus, remember?

273
00:17:31,252 --> 00:17:33,625
I was waiting for you, but you never came,
so I came for you.

274
00:17:33,625 --> 00:17:35,905
Why are you guys here?

275
00:17:35,905 --> 00:17:37,203
Are you feeling okay?

276
00:17:37,203 --> 00:17:39,747
No broken bones? No injuries?

277
00:17:39,747 --> 00:17:41,305
I'm fine.

278
00:17:42,125 --> 00:17:44,703
Hey. What's wrong with Ha Na?

279
00:17:49,076 --> 00:17:52,030
What's up with you?

280
00:18:13,123 --> 00:18:14,381
Three...

281
00:18:14,381 --> 00:18:15,501
Two...

282
00:18:15,501 --> 00:18:17,388
One! There it is.

283
00:18:17,388 --> 00:18:19,088
Happy New Year, guys!

284
00:18:20,228 --> 00:18:21,754
I guess.

285
00:18:24,118 --> 00:18:25,906
Hey, what's going on with you, Yoon Ha Ru?

286
00:18:25,906 --> 00:18:28,233
Why are you so unenthusiastic?

287
00:18:30,918 --> 00:18:33,809
Oh, am I supposed to be doing something?

288
00:18:33,809 --> 00:18:35,188
Well, no.

289
00:18:35,188 --> 00:18:37,422
Not really, I guess.

290
00:18:37,422 --> 00:18:40,141
This is so fun!

291
00:18:40,141 --> 00:18:41,257
Yeah, guys!

292
00:18:41,257 --> 00:18:43,504
Let's have a super happy new year!
Lots of luck for everyone!

293
00:18:43,504 --> 00:18:44,709
We're seniors now, seniors!

294
00:18:44,709 --> 00:18:47,029
We're 19 years old now!

295
00:18:48,519 --> 00:18:51,042
- What's up with Ha Na today?
- This is so awesome!

296
00:18:51,042 --> 00:18:52,742
I don't know.

297
00:18:53,698 --> 00:18:57,041
She's acting a bit strange today.

298
00:18:57,903 --> 00:18:59,971
Watch your step!

299
00:19:05,423 --> 00:19:07,496
She's adorable.

300
00:19:07,496 --> 00:19:09,481
- What?
- She's...

301
00:19:11,259 --> 00:19:13,445
No... nothing...

302
00:19:13,445 --> 00:19:15,825
Ha Na. She's...

303
00:19:15,825 --> 00:19:18,210
I said she's being particularly silly today.

304
00:19:18,210 --> 00:19:19,721
See? It's ridiculous.

305
00:19:19,721 --> 00:19:21,798
Something's up with her today.

306
00:19:21,798 --> 00:19:23,855
She's just being so silly today.

307
00:19:26,619 --> 00:19:28,479
Come on, this way!

308
00:19:28,479 --> 00:19:30,179
Alright, alright!

309
00:19:34,660 --> 00:19:35,798
Hey.

310
00:19:35,798 --> 00:19:37,498
Keep it together, will you?

311
00:19:38,528 --> 00:19:39,630
You're Yoon Ha Na now.

312
00:19:39,630 --> 00:19:42,241
Yoon Ha Na, the world-famous actress,
not the wild beast Yoon Ha Ru.

313
00:19:42,241 --> 00:19:44,015
I know!

314
00:19:44,015 --> 00:19:45,545
Woo Jae is giving you weird looks!

315
00:19:45,545 --> 00:19:47,471
Stop acting like an imbecile!

316
00:19:47,471 --> 00:19:48,619
Imbecile?

317
00:19:48,619 --> 00:19:50,140
I'm the national judo team's treasure,

318
00:19:50,140 --> 00:19:53,337
and the world's best judo player,
Sir Yoon Ha Ru!

319
00:20:00,601 --> 00:20:02,729
You should try your best to act like yourself,

320
00:20:02,729 --> 00:20:05,232
and I as myself, don't you think?

321
00:20:05,846 --> 00:20:06,954
Hey, you.

322
00:20:06,954 --> 00:20:08,642
Are you embarrassed by me or something?

323
00:20:08,642 --> 00:20:12,290
Of course I am, what kind of question is that?
You're acting out of character in my body!

324
00:20:16,859 --> 00:20:18,743
Besides...

325
00:20:20,733 --> 00:20:22,433
I'm just scared.

326
00:20:23,674 --> 00:20:25,610
What if some small action...

327
00:20:26,645 --> 00:20:30,557
ends up irreversibly changing our past?

328
00:20:31,144 --> 00:20:32,270
You know.

329
00:20:32,270 --> 00:20:33,381
That's how it goes in movies.

330
00:20:33,381 --> 00:20:36,225
Just think about how the medal changed.

331
00:20:36,225 --> 00:20:39,497
We can save Jung Woo Jae.

332
00:20:43,792 --> 00:20:45,250
Okay.

333
00:21:01,568 --> 00:21:04,518
You must've been starving.

334
00:21:07,941 --> 00:21:10,485
Hey, will you slow down?

335
00:21:10,485 --> 00:21:13,405
All this food you're shoveling
in your mouth right now...

336
00:21:14,229 --> 00:21:16,100
are you even keeping track
of how many calories that is?

337
00:21:16,100 --> 00:21:17,268
This is my first meal of the day!

338
00:21:17,268 --> 00:21:20,325
I'll just work out and burn it off,
so stop nagging me!

339
00:21:23,347 --> 00:21:24,684
You should slow down, though.

340
00:21:24,684 --> 00:21:26,384
Here, drink some water, too.

341
00:21:31,546 --> 00:21:32,660
Guys...

342
00:21:32,660 --> 00:21:34,478
I need to use the toilet.

343
00:21:34,478 --> 00:21:36,424
Agh, I'm about to poop my pants!

344
00:21:38,031 --> 00:21:40,053
What, right now? It's dangerous in the dark.

345
00:21:40,053 --> 00:21:43,209
- Do you want me to come with?
- Stop talking, it's peeking out!

346
00:21:43,807 --> 00:21:44,913
Ha Na!

347
00:21:44,913 --> 00:21:47,378
What does he think he's doing?

348
00:21:54,025 --> 00:21:56,083
Ha Na! That's the men's room!

349
00:21:58,179 --> 00:22:00,208
No, no, I told you I'm not drunk!

350
00:22:00,208 --> 00:22:01,543
I'm not drunk, I'm fine...

351
00:22:01,543 --> 00:22:03,499
Stop there for a second.

352
00:22:03,499 --> 00:22:05,178
All the toilets are backed up.

353
00:22:05,178 --> 00:22:06,595
Everything's broken in there.

354
00:22:06,595 --> 00:22:07,943
Sorry for the inconvenience.

355
00:22:07,943 --> 00:22:10,249
Did I poop too much? What if I clogged it?

356
00:22:24,538 --> 00:22:26,929
<i>I don't know what Jung Woo Jae is wishing for,</i>

357
00:22:26,929 --> 00:22:28,199
<i>but whatever it is...</i>

358
00:22:28,199 --> 00:22:30,289
<i>I wish for it to come true.</i>

359
00:22:30,289 --> 00:22:31,509
<i>Please...</i>

360
00:22:31,509 --> 00:22:33,061
<i>Please.</i>

361
00:22:40,834 --> 00:22:42,711
What did you wish for?

362
00:22:42,711 --> 00:22:44,181
Hey! You're not supposed to tell.

363
00:22:44,181 --> 00:22:45,302
It won't come true!

364
00:22:45,302 --> 00:22:47,565
That's not how it works.

365
00:22:47,565 --> 00:22:50,621
Come on, tell me.
I could help make it come true.

366
00:22:52,334 --> 00:22:54,598
Well, I suppose you could help, yeah.

367
00:22:54,598 --> 00:22:56,261
What is it?

368
00:22:56,261 --> 00:22:58,132
The national team trial
is being held this year.

369
00:22:58,132 --> 00:23:00,172
I want to make it on the team with you.

370
00:23:00,172 --> 00:23:01,572
Yoon Ha Ru.

371
00:23:03,158 --> 00:23:04,748
- Huh?
- Well? Answer me.

372
00:23:04,748 --> 00:23:05,979
Don't you want to?

373
00:23:05,979 --> 00:23:08,562
- Well...
- Of course!

374
00:23:09,749 --> 00:23:11,180
Don't even worry about it!

375
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:15,102
You and I, we'll make it in. Whatever it takes.

376
00:23:15,102 --> 00:23:16,566
Huh? Ha Na?

377
00:23:16,566 --> 00:23:18,266
What do you mean, you and me?

378
00:23:20,123 --> 00:23:21,394
Oh, no, no.

379
00:23:21,394 --> 00:23:23,144
I meant, you and Yoon Ha Ru. You two.

380
00:23:23,144 --> 00:23:24,844
You'll make it in.

381
00:23:25,646 --> 00:23:27,346
You got me there.

382
00:23:40,235 --> 00:23:41,992
About Woo Jae...

383
00:23:41,992 --> 00:23:44,208
When did he stop judo again?

384
00:23:44,817 --> 00:23:48,342
Right before the national team trial, so...

385
00:23:48,342 --> 00:23:50,578
I guess around May?

386
00:23:50,578 --> 00:23:52,275
He hurt his shoulder.

387
00:23:52,275 --> 00:23:53,906
That's why he quit, right?

388
00:23:53,906 --> 00:23:55,774
Did it happen during practice?

389
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:58,118
I think...

390
00:23:58,118 --> 00:24:00,678
He just appeared with a cast
on his arm one day.

391
00:24:02,334 --> 00:24:03,929
Are you sure you're a good friend to him?

392
00:24:03,929 --> 00:24:05,609
You're his friend, too, you know!

393
00:24:05,609 --> 00:24:07,309
But you had no clue, either!

394
00:24:09,722 --> 00:24:11,117
Well, this time around...

395
00:24:11,117 --> 00:24:13,487
Let's figure that out first.

396
00:24:13,487 --> 00:24:15,330
And then what?

397
00:24:15,330 --> 00:24:17,514
That way, we can prevent it from happening.

398
00:24:17,514 --> 00:24:19,451
That way...

399
00:24:19,451 --> 00:24:22,042
he'll never have to quit judo.

400
00:24:25,031 --> 00:24:26,688
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

401
00:24:26,688 --> 00:24:28,040
Okay.

402
00:24:39,725 --> 00:24:44,586
[Our dream, a brighter 2011]

403
00:24:46,853 --> 00:24:48,553
It's good.

404
00:24:51,169 --> 00:24:52,507
Oh, you're back.

405
00:24:52,507 --> 00:24:54,878
Wow, Woo Jae! How handsome you are!

406
00:24:54,878 --> 00:24:56,415
What a charming young man!

407
00:24:56,415 --> 00:24:57,604
Honey, what about me?

408
00:24:57,604 --> 00:24:59,681
Am I charming, too?

409
00:25:01,739 --> 00:25:03,270
I guess not.

410
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:04,822
Anyhow!

411
00:25:04,822 --> 00:25:06,528
Did you guys enjoy the sunrise?

412
00:25:06,528 --> 00:25:07,739
Did you take pictures?

413
00:25:07,739 --> 00:25:09,939
Wash your hands, your dad made tteokguk.

414
00:25:09,939 --> 00:25:11,679
- Mom!
- Dad!

415
00:25:11,679 --> 00:25:13,016
What is it now?

416
00:25:13,016 --> 00:25:14,231
Don't you like it?

417
00:25:14,231 --> 00:25:15,513
I did a good job on it.

418
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:16,867
No, it's not that.

419
00:25:16,867 --> 00:25:20,673
I can't believe how the two of you look!

420
00:25:20,673 --> 00:25:22,680
This is unreal!

421
00:25:22,680 --> 00:25:24,173
This is just...

422
00:25:24,173 --> 00:25:25,687
Mom, your skin!

423
00:25:25,687 --> 00:25:29,284
Holy moly guacamole, that's gnarly!

424
00:25:30,993 --> 00:25:33,049
What did you say? Hole-y? Mole-y?

425
00:25:33,049 --> 00:25:34,771
And what, gnarled?

426
00:25:34,771 --> 00:25:36,847
Not you too, Ha Na!

427
00:25:36,847 --> 00:25:39,234
No, Mom! It's a compliment! A compliment!

428
00:25:39,234 --> 00:25:40,650
Yoon Ha Na, come here!

429
00:25:40,650 --> 00:25:41,674
I said come here!

430
00:25:41,674 --> 00:25:43,786
Did you take after Ha Ru?

431
00:25:43,786 --> 00:25:45,144
Huh? Come here!

432
00:25:45,144 --> 00:25:46,846
- Mom, Mom!
- How dare you call me gnarled!

433
00:25:46,846 --> 00:25:48,027
- It's a compliment!
- Come here right now!

434
00:25:48,027 --> 00:25:50,071
- No, I was complimenting you!
- It's a compliment...

435
00:25:50,071 --> 00:25:51,771
Eat up, everyone.

436
00:25:52,927 --> 00:25:55,156
Woah, it's gosh dang tummylicious!

437
00:25:56,461 --> 00:25:57,832
Yoon Ha Na!

438
00:25:57,832 --> 00:26:00,085
What do you mean by that now?

439
00:26:01,354 --> 00:26:02,783
It means it's really good.

440
00:26:02,783 --> 00:26:03,807
It's just what we say.

441
00:26:03,807 --> 00:26:05,127
Yeah, that's right.

442
00:26:05,127 --> 00:26:07,211
- Is this true?
- Yes.

443
00:26:09,561 --> 00:26:11,394
Come on, honey.

444
00:26:11,394 --> 00:26:12,418
It's just how kids are.

445
00:26:12,418 --> 00:26:14,354
We were young once, too, right?

446
00:26:14,354 --> 00:26:16,207
It's just how teens talk. Their lingo.

447
00:26:16,207 --> 00:26:17,601
They'll grow out of it.

448
00:26:17,601 --> 00:26:19,861
"Grow out of it?"

449
00:26:19,861 --> 00:26:22,407
You still say stuff like rad and bonkers.

450
00:26:22,407 --> 00:26:24,814
- Old habits die hard, and...
- Oh, look, meat fritters.

451
00:26:24,814 --> 00:26:27,089
Your favorite, see?

452
00:26:29,360 --> 00:26:32,134
Aw, you look lovely when you eat.

453
00:26:32,134 --> 00:26:33,834
It tastes great, yes.

454
00:26:34,613 --> 00:26:35,637
- Dad.
- Yes?

455
00:26:35,637 --> 00:26:37,048
This is an amazing meal.

456
00:26:37,048 --> 00:26:39,207
Well, I am a good cook, see?

457
00:26:39,207 --> 00:26:40,781
What do you guys think? Am I rad?

458
00:26:40,781 --> 00:26:42,628
Yeah, radical!

459
00:26:42,628 --> 00:26:44,081
Bonkers!

460
00:26:44,081 --> 00:26:45,574
Ha Ru, did you finish packing yet?

461
00:26:45,574 --> 00:26:47,435
Packing? For what?

462
00:26:49,968 --> 00:26:52,121
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru.

463
00:26:52,121 --> 00:26:54,499
You're leaving for the
training camp in two days!

464
00:26:54,499 --> 00:26:56,265
I told you to get ready beforehand!

465
00:26:56,265 --> 00:26:58,205
You never listen, do you?

466
00:26:58,205 --> 00:27:00,581
Hurry up and finish eating! You need to pack!

467
00:27:02,612 --> 00:27:05,446
Honey, calm down and have another fritter...

468
00:27:06,099 --> 00:27:08,223
Oh, you've already got one.

469
00:27:09,214 --> 00:27:11,745
<i>You should tell me right away
if you changed your number.</i>

470
00:27:11,745 --> 00:27:14,108
<i>Son. Where are you?</i>

471
00:27:16,362 --> 00:27:18,062
[Haesol High Judo Team Winter Camp]
Attention!

472
00:27:18,826 --> 00:27:21,652
There is only one goal
in this winter training camp.

473
00:27:21,652 --> 00:27:23,179
You are not only a team on the mat.

474
00:27:23,179 --> 00:27:26,458
You will eat, sleep, and even use the toilet...
as if you are one single organism.

475
00:27:26,458 --> 00:27:29,491
Therefore, you will stay in rooms of four.
No exceptions.

476
00:27:29,491 --> 00:27:31,066
- Oh, crap.
- Any objections?

477
00:27:31,066 --> 00:27:32,483
- No, sir!
- No, sir!

478
00:27:32,483 --> 00:27:35,808
Good. Now, take off to unpack and settle in.
You will return here after 30 minutes.

479
00:27:35,808 --> 00:27:36,865
Understood?

480
00:27:36,865 --> 00:27:38,565
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

481
00:27:42,319 --> 00:27:44,019
We're in the same room.

482
00:27:44,851 --> 00:27:46,219
Oh, okay...

483
00:27:46,219 --> 00:27:47,602
Us, too.

484
00:27:55,131 --> 00:27:56,395
<i>Hey, Yoon Ha Na.</i>

485
00:27:56,395 --> 00:27:57,839
<i>Listen up carefully.</i>

486
00:27:57,839 --> 00:28:01,552
<i>Where you will be going tomorrow
is no ordinary training camp.</i>

487
00:28:01,552 --> 00:28:04,741
<i>That place is like the wilderness.
A safari, if you will.</i>

488
00:28:05,332 --> 00:28:06,356
<i>A safari?</i>

489
00:28:06,356 --> 00:28:07,384
<i>But do not fear!</i>

490
00:28:07,384 --> 00:28:11,529
<i>For I, your big brother, will teach you
all the essentials of survival.</i>

491
00:28:11,529 --> 00:28:12,859
<i>First off.</i>

492
00:28:12,859 --> 00:28:14,978
<i>The smell.</i>

493
00:28:14,978 --> 00:28:16,148
<i>Smell?</i>

494
00:28:16,148 --> 00:28:17,925
<i>The moment you set foot in that room...</i>

495
00:28:17,925 --> 00:28:21,036
<i>you will learn what hell is like.</i>

496
00:28:21,880 --> 00:28:23,270
<i>You've got to be exaggerating.</i>

497
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:25,342
<i>You know Han Soo Hyuk, right?</i>

498
00:28:25,342 --> 00:28:26,996
<i>Han Soo Hyuk?</i>

499
00:28:28,109 --> 00:28:31,155
<i>The guy who quit judo
and came to my university...</i>

500
00:28:31,155 --> 00:28:32,195
<i>That Han Soo Hyuk?</i>

501
00:28:32,195 --> 00:28:33,305
<i>Well? What about him?</i>

502
00:28:33,305 --> 00:28:35,416
<i>What does he have to do with this?</i>

503
00:28:40,665 --> 00:28:43,139
<i>If you are condemned to a room with him...</i>

504
00:28:43,139 --> 00:28:45,581
<i>Well, you truly are doomed.</i>

505
00:28:53,390 --> 00:28:55,258
[Alarms off, please!]

506
00:28:55,282 --> 00:28:56,819
[Han Soo Hyuk]
[Yoon Ha Ru]

507
00:29:11,428 --> 00:29:12,972
What's wrong?

508
00:29:12,972 --> 00:29:15,972
<i>He has rhinitis, so his nose is always stuffy,
and he can't smell very well.</i>

509
00:29:15,972 --> 00:29:17,379
<i>Maybe that's why, but...</i>

510
00:29:17,379 --> 00:29:18,896
You!

511
00:29:19,552 --> 00:29:21,818
When did you last wash your uniform?

512
00:29:24,071 --> 00:29:25,095
Hey.

513
00:29:25,095 --> 00:29:26,753
Want a bite?

514
00:29:26,753 --> 00:29:28,579
<i>He doesn't do his laundry.</i>

515
00:29:28,579 --> 00:29:29,911
<i>As you already know, however...</i>

516
00:29:29,911 --> 00:29:31,719
<i>He's a good kid.</i>

517
00:29:31,719 --> 00:29:32,628
It's good bread.

518
00:29:32,628 --> 00:29:33,632
<i>And now.</i>

519
00:29:33,632 --> 00:29:35,978
<i>Pyo Gyeong Woo.</i>

520
00:29:35,978 --> 00:29:37,455
<i>I know Gyeong Woo.</i>

521
00:29:37,455 --> 00:29:40,348
<i>He's the son of the master
of that training center we went to as children.</i>

522
00:29:40,348 --> 00:29:43,535
<i>Starting tomorrow,
your eyes will be forced to witness...</i>

523
00:29:43,535 --> 00:29:45,596
<i>the parade of muscles.</i>

524
00:29:45,596 --> 00:29:47,725
<i>"Parade of muscles?"</i>

525
00:29:48,744 --> 00:29:50,962
- Get it out of my face.
- But it's really good.

526
00:30:08,407 --> 00:30:09,449
What...

527
00:30:09,449 --> 00:30:11,011
What are you doing?

528
00:30:13,408 --> 00:30:14,679
Hey.

529
00:30:16,043 --> 00:30:19,586
Pyo Gyeong Woo, sir,
reporting today's sick gains.

530
00:30:22,350 --> 00:30:24,252
- What's going on?
- How do you like them?

531
00:30:24,252 --> 00:30:26,157
<i>Our dear Gyeong Woo is, how should I say this?</i>

532
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:28,124
<i>He's like a big dog who likes praise.</i>

533
00:30:28,124 --> 00:30:29,614
<i>Just think of him as that.</i>

534
00:30:29,614 --> 00:30:31,145
<i>He's a good kid, too. He doesn't mean any harm.</i>

535
00:30:31,145 --> 00:30:33,070
Here, my external oblique. Feel it.

536
00:30:33,070 --> 00:30:34,139
Come on, won't you feel it?

537
00:30:34,139 --> 00:30:35,839
My rectus abdominis...

538
00:30:37,989 --> 00:30:40,573
I've been doing low-rises...

539
00:30:47,707 --> 00:30:49,407
Salute!

540
00:30:57,700 --> 00:30:59,163
Oh, hello.

541
00:31:00,506 --> 00:31:02,206
Hello.

542
00:31:07,409 --> 00:31:08,973
<i>Also,</i>

543
00:31:08,973 --> 00:31:10,854
<i>this is the most important of them all.</i>

544
00:31:11,529 --> 00:31:12,673
<i>There's more?</i>

545
00:31:12,673 --> 00:31:14,506
<i>Jung Woo Jae.</i>

546
00:31:15,952 --> 00:31:17,629
<i>Keep an eye on him.</i>

547
00:31:17,629 --> 00:31:19,560
<i>If he's secretive, dig deeper.</i>

548
00:31:19,560 --> 00:31:21,800
<i>If he says he's fine, don't believe him.</i>

549
00:31:23,229 --> 00:31:24,933
<i>This time...</i>

550
00:31:24,933 --> 00:31:27,508
<i>We need to figure it out faster than him.</i>

551
00:31:27,508 --> 00:31:28,532
<i>Okay.</i>

552
00:31:28,532 --> 00:31:29,702
<i>Got it?</i>

553
00:31:29,702 --> 00:31:30,926
<i>Yeah.</i>

554
00:31:30,926 --> 00:31:32,793
<i>Are you done packing?</i>

555
00:31:32,793 --> 00:31:34,551
<i>What good is that going to do?</i>

556
00:31:34,551 --> 00:31:36,085
<i>Don't take hour-long showers
while you're there, understood?</i>

557
00:31:36,085 --> 00:31:38,879
<i>I just take longer showers than most, okay?</i>

558
00:31:38,879 --> 00:31:42,290
<i>Take stuff like this, for working out.</i>

559
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:47,419
<i>You can keep this stuff for yourself.</i>

560
00:32:13,242 --> 00:32:15,013
<i>This time...</i>

561
00:32:15,013 --> 00:32:18,256
<i>I swear I'll protect you, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

562
00:32:24,490 --> 00:32:27,665
[Haesol High Judo Team Winter Camp]

563
00:32:52,314 --> 00:32:54,972
Agh, what are you doing?

564
00:33:09,587 --> 00:33:11,334
<i>Jung Woo Jae...</i>

565
00:33:21,090 --> 00:33:22,147
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!

566
00:33:22,147 --> 00:33:23,998
Get it together!

567
00:33:31,639 --> 00:33:33,512
[Quitters are never winners!]

568
00:33:40,493 --> 00:33:43,033
Your skills... are getting better!

569
00:33:43,033 --> 00:33:45,485
It's getting better by the minute! Good!

570
00:33:45,485 --> 00:33:48,414
- What a monster!
- That must be stressful.

571
00:33:48,414 --> 00:33:49,868
You're getting better!

572
00:33:49,868 --> 00:33:51,410
Come on, believe it!

573
00:33:51,410 --> 00:33:53,151
It's like a whole truck is on top of you.

574
00:33:53,151 --> 00:33:54,891
This is how you learn, you hear me?

575
00:33:54,891 --> 00:33:56,940
This is how you learn!

576
00:33:58,634 --> 00:34:01,165
Look, guys, Woo Jae is having
a great workout sesh!

577
00:34:03,846 --> 00:34:05,355
Yoon Ha Ru!

578
00:34:06,194 --> 00:34:07,894
You've got that glint in your eyes.

579
00:34:09,859 --> 00:34:11,390
Come here.

580
00:34:11,390 --> 00:34:12,741
Come on, hurry up.

581
00:34:12,741 --> 00:34:14,834
Looks refreshing.

582
00:34:14,834 --> 00:34:17,041
- You have to go.
- No, but...

583
00:34:17,041 --> 00:34:18,335
- Hurry up.
- You have no choice.

584
00:34:18,335 --> 00:34:19,363
- Quickly, now.
- Goodbye.

585
00:34:19,363 --> 00:34:22,013
- Hurry, now.
- Good luck!

586
00:34:22,013 --> 00:34:23,713
Yoon Ha Ru.

587
00:34:35,388 --> 00:34:37,165
What is wrong with you?

588
00:34:37,165 --> 00:34:38,582
Get out of here.

589
00:34:39,260 --> 00:34:40,437
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

590
00:34:40,437 --> 00:34:41,652
Are you alright?

591
00:34:41,652 --> 00:34:43,954
What were you thinking?

592
00:34:43,954 --> 00:34:45,175
What's the matter?

593
00:34:45,175 --> 00:34:48,777
- Did I do something wrong?
- You just got pummeled into the ground!

594
00:34:48,777 --> 00:34:50,707
He armlocked you!

595
00:34:50,707 --> 00:34:52,788
What do you think you're doing?

596
00:34:52,788 --> 00:34:55,281
What do you mean? I'm training.

597
00:34:55,281 --> 00:34:56,737
Are you injured?

598
00:34:56,737 --> 00:34:58,494
Move your shoulder like this. Does it hurt?

599
00:34:58,494 --> 00:35:00,410
Hey, look, I'm fine!

600
00:35:01,062 --> 00:35:02,086
Hey!

601
00:35:02,086 --> 00:35:03,394
Take good care of your shoulder!

602
00:35:03,394 --> 00:35:04,862
Just be gentle with it, okay?

603
00:35:04,862 --> 00:35:06,441
- Wait, what's wrong?
- Are you hurt?

604
00:35:06,441 --> 00:35:07,806
- Where?
- Is something wrong?

605
00:35:07,806 --> 00:35:09,690
I'm fine.

606
00:35:09,690 --> 00:35:11,527
- Get out of my way.
- Hey, but your shoulder...

607
00:35:11,527 --> 00:35:13,260
He's clearly injured...

608
00:35:14,394 --> 00:35:16,094
Right?

609
00:35:25,038 --> 00:35:27,252
What, is this seriously all you're eating?

610
00:35:27,951 --> 00:35:29,525
Yes. What's wrong?

611
00:35:29,525 --> 00:35:31,913
This isn't enough food for an athlete.

612
00:35:31,913 --> 00:35:33,100
I think it's perfect.

613
00:35:33,100 --> 00:35:36,192
What's up with you, man?

614
00:35:36,192 --> 00:35:37,892
No, why do you ask?

615
00:35:39,053 --> 00:35:40,398
Nothing.

616
00:35:46,700 --> 00:35:48,656
[Dad]

617
00:35:59,110 --> 00:36:00,158
Hey.

618
00:36:00,158 --> 00:36:01,402
Oh, wow, hello!

619
00:36:01,402 --> 00:36:04,553
Hi! Hi, everyone.

620
00:36:07,049 --> 00:36:09,044
<i>I'm at the school. Come outside.</i>

621
00:36:09,044 --> 00:36:10,370
So tasty!

622
00:36:32,830 --> 00:36:34,350
Hey! Son!

623
00:36:34,350 --> 00:36:36,050
Son, hey! Come here!

624
00:36:44,954 --> 00:36:47,780
There are too many people around. Come with me.

625
00:36:49,370 --> 00:36:50,717
Wow, the bastard.

626
00:36:50,717 --> 00:36:53,391
So rude to his own father.

627
00:37:04,739 --> 00:37:06,874
- Where are they going?
- I don't know.

628
00:37:09,744 --> 00:37:12,418
My son. It's so hard to see you these days.

629
00:37:13,928 --> 00:37:15,587
How did you find out about this place?

630
00:37:15,587 --> 00:37:16,775
What? How did I find out?

631
00:37:16,775 --> 00:37:18,557
You know my friend, Mr. Jung Gyu, right?

632
00:37:18,557 --> 00:37:21,763
Well, he told me you were in the newspaper!

633
00:37:23,174 --> 00:37:25,064
See this? "The future of Korea.

634
00:37:25,064 --> 00:37:27,535
Rising stars of the national team..."

635
00:37:27,535 --> 00:37:28,584
And here, here. Look.

636
00:37:28,584 --> 00:37:31,170
"Haesol High, Judo Team, 11th grader...

637
00:37:31,170 --> 00:37:33,468
Jung Woo Jae."

638
00:37:34,253 --> 00:37:35,870
Now, isn't that something?

639
00:37:35,870 --> 00:37:37,647
Wow, so, whose son is that, I wonder?

640
00:37:37,647 --> 00:37:39,580
Am I right?

641
00:37:44,641 --> 00:37:46,341
So, where's your mom?

642
00:37:47,199 --> 00:37:48,510
Why do you want to know?

643
00:37:48,510 --> 00:37:49,621
"Why?"

644
00:37:49,621 --> 00:37:53,101
So I'm just supposed to let that fox
live happily ever after without me?

645
00:37:55,312 --> 00:37:57,124
I don't know.

646
00:37:57,124 --> 00:37:58,461
We haven't kept in touch for a while.

647
00:37:58,461 --> 00:38:00,828
You little liar.

648
00:38:01,426 --> 00:38:03,830
You go and tell that woman, you hear me?

649
00:38:03,830 --> 00:38:05,458
Tell her that she'll never hide from me.

650
00:38:05,458 --> 00:38:07,781
I'll find her, just you wait.

651
00:38:07,781 --> 00:38:09,032
And you.

652
00:38:09,032 --> 00:38:10,732
Got some cash?

653
00:38:14,621 --> 00:38:18,239
The article said you're
getting good financial support.

654
00:38:18,239 --> 00:38:19,877
Nothing? Really?

655
00:38:19,877 --> 00:38:21,453
Do you think I owe you anything?

656
00:38:21,453 --> 00:38:23,826
Think, now. Have you ever given me anything?

657
00:38:23,826 --> 00:38:26,460
- That's no way to talk to your dad!
- "Dad?"

658
00:38:26,460 --> 00:38:29,047
If you want me to treat you like a father,

659
00:38:29,047 --> 00:38:31,092
don't ever go looking for Mom.

660
00:38:31,741 --> 00:38:33,540
I'm warning you.

661
00:38:41,557 --> 00:38:43,807
That's everything I have.

662
00:38:43,807 --> 00:38:45,439
So just please,

663
00:38:45,439 --> 00:38:46,816
don't ever come see me again.

664
00:38:46,816 --> 00:38:48,994
Rude little rascal.

665
00:38:48,994 --> 00:38:50,437
See you.

666
00:39:04,061 --> 00:39:07,944
- Why are you making weird noises?
- This is a good stretch!

667
00:39:15,717 --> 00:39:17,839
- Come on, faster.
- Yes, sir.

668
00:39:17,839 --> 00:39:19,168
Let's go.

669
00:39:20,737 --> 00:39:21,951
Let's do 10 sets of 400.

670
00:39:21,951 --> 00:39:23,481
- Boo!
- No!

671
00:39:23,481 --> 00:39:24,922
- What even!
- Boo! Boo!

672
00:39:24,922 --> 00:39:25,946
Okay, then, 15 sets it is.

673
00:39:25,946 --> 00:39:30,273
- 10 sets is good!
- Yay, 10! We'll do our best!

674
00:39:31,751 --> 00:39:33,475
- All good?
- Yes, sir!

675
00:39:33,475 --> 00:39:36,042
If Soo Hyuk falls behind,
I'll make all of you do 4 more sets,

676
00:39:36,042 --> 00:39:38,573
so keep encouraging him, okay?

677
00:39:39,375 --> 00:39:40,653
I'll carry him on my back!

678
00:39:40,653 --> 00:39:42,466
- Pass it on.
- Ready, set...

679
00:39:52,343 --> 00:39:54,043
This is nice.

680
00:39:58,856 --> 00:40:00,434
<i>Do you think I owe you anything?</i>

681
00:40:00,434 --> 00:40:02,808
<i>Have you ever given me anything?</i>

682
00:40:02,808 --> 00:40:05,449
<i>- That's no way to talk to your dad!
- "Dad?"</i>

683
00:40:05,449 --> 00:40:08,043
<i>If you want me to treat you like a father,</i>

684
00:40:08,043 --> 00:40:10,128
<i>don't ever go looking for Mom.</i>

685
00:40:13,455 --> 00:40:15,155
Time for exercise.

686
00:40:25,176 --> 00:40:28,318
I can't do anything with
Yoon Ha Na's feeble body!

687
00:40:28,318 --> 00:40:30,685
What am I supposed to do in this body?

688
00:40:33,705 --> 00:40:35,589
Think, Yoon Ha Ru.

689
00:40:35,589 --> 00:40:37,563
What can I do in this situation?

690
00:40:37,563 --> 00:40:39,842
Come up with something, anything, Yoon Ha Ru!

691
00:40:40,629 --> 00:40:42,066
- Bye!
- Goodbye!

692
00:40:42,066 --> 00:40:43,150
- What are we having?
- Pork belly!

693
00:40:43,150 --> 00:40:46,077
- Grilled pork belly!
- Pork belly, pork, pork!

694
00:40:53,555 --> 00:40:55,501
Hey, what are you doing? Come out already!

695
00:40:55,501 --> 00:40:57,152
I'm coming, okay?
I think the makchang I had was bad.

696
00:40:57,152 --> 00:40:58,192
I got a bellyache.

697
00:40:58,192 --> 00:40:59,749
You're pissing me off.

698
00:40:59,749 --> 00:41:01,405
<i>It's out of my system now.</i>

699
00:41:01,405 --> 00:41:04,055
- Hey, Woo Jae, do you have time to...
- Oh!

700
00:41:04,769 --> 00:41:06,400
The walking 500 million won.

701
00:41:10,549 --> 00:41:12,661
- Woo Jae...
- Hey! Come to the back gate!

702
00:41:12,661 --> 00:41:14,021
Back gate?

703
00:41:14,021 --> 00:41:15,721
Okay, on it!

704
00:41:22,794 --> 00:41:24,834
Hey! Stop right there, money-maker!

705
00:41:30,036 --> 00:41:31,400
Hey!

706
00:41:32,327 --> 00:41:34,027
Hey! Come here!

707
00:41:43,843 --> 00:41:45,981
Why are there so many damn stairs?

708
00:42:19,953 --> 00:42:21,334
[Location information act]

709
00:42:21,334 --> 00:42:24,320
"Threatening for money is extortion,
a criminal offense..."

710
00:42:24,320 --> 00:42:27,420
"Tracking someone's location
is against the law..."

711
00:42:27,420 --> 00:42:30,265
So it's a felony, huh?

712
00:42:32,162 --> 00:42:34,204
<i>You go and tell that woman, you hear me?</i>

713
00:42:34,204 --> 00:42:35,825
<i>Tell her that she'll never hide from me.</i>

714
00:42:35,825 --> 00:42:38,134
<i>Oh, I'll find her, just you wait.</i>

715
00:42:38,134 --> 00:42:39,398
<i>And you.</i>

716
00:42:39,398 --> 00:42:41,098
<i>Got some cash?</i>

717
00:42:41,904 --> 00:42:44,989
Can he file a restraining order or something?

718
00:42:48,411 --> 00:42:50,139
[Ask a lawyer online]

719
00:42:50,139 --> 00:42:53,008
[Underage son...]

720
00:42:56,081 --> 00:42:57,175
[Beast]

721
00:42:58,409 --> 00:43:00,109
Wow, that's rich.

722
00:43:00,699 --> 00:43:02,990
Yes, this is the mangy beast speaking.

723
00:43:02,990 --> 00:43:04,141
<i>So, what did you find out?</i>

724
00:43:04,141 --> 00:43:05,325
Woo Jae...

725
00:43:05,325 --> 00:43:06,646
<i>Woo Jae is...</i>

726
00:43:06,646 --> 00:43:09,091
Well? Spit it out! What's wrong with Woo Jae?

727
00:43:24,439 --> 00:43:26,139
You little...

728
00:43:30,758 --> 00:43:31,825
I'm here.

729
00:43:31,825 --> 00:43:33,525
Where are you?

730
00:43:34,626 --> 00:43:35,970
I lost them.

731
00:43:35,970 --> 00:43:37,207
They're nowhere to be seen!

732
00:43:37,207 --> 00:43:39,169
I'm certain they went this way!

733
00:43:39,169 --> 00:43:42,566
Some sketchy men said
Woo Jae is worth 500 million won.

734
00:43:42,566 --> 00:43:44,416
<i>They were chasing him around, and...</i>

735
00:43:44,416 --> 00:43:46,116
What do we do?

736
00:43:46,803 --> 00:43:48,800
- Yoon Ha Na.
- Yes?

737
00:43:48,800 --> 00:43:50,708
<i>Listen carefully.</i>

738
00:43:50,708 --> 00:43:52,798
Haesol is a small city.
We'll find them sooner or later.

739
00:43:52,798 --> 00:43:54,091
Okay.

740
00:43:56,108 --> 00:43:57,808
Damn it!

741
00:44:19,680 --> 00:44:21,627
Come here, you little rat!

742
00:44:21,627 --> 00:44:23,327
Come here!

743
00:44:29,129 --> 00:44:30,652
Get out of the way!

744
00:44:33,842 --> 00:44:35,542
Get over here!

745
00:44:41,469 --> 00:44:43,753
Stop there, you bastard!

746
00:44:59,502 --> 00:45:00,930
Oh, sir!

747
00:45:04,922 --> 00:45:06,622
You're dead now.

748
00:45:20,635 --> 00:45:22,335
It's been a while, huh?

749
00:45:34,861 --> 00:45:36,356
How did you find me this time?

750
00:45:36,356 --> 00:45:37,831
How did I find you?

751
00:45:37,831 --> 00:45:40,354
Well, the answer's obvious, isn't it?

752
00:45:40,354 --> 00:45:42,510
Your dad, of course!

753
00:45:42,510 --> 00:45:44,918
He literally pointed me to where you are.

754
00:45:49,330 --> 00:45:50,388
I...

755
00:45:50,388 --> 00:45:52,731
I don't want anything to do with him.

756
00:45:53,390 --> 00:45:55,870
- Just let me go.
- Wow, just wow.

757
00:45:55,870 --> 00:45:57,570
You're an athlete, right?

758
00:45:58,466 --> 00:46:00,566
You're well-recognized, too, isn't that so?

759
00:46:00,566 --> 00:46:03,402
I heard you receive good sponsorship.

760
00:46:04,886 --> 00:46:06,996
- That's not true.
- Don't lie to me.

761
00:46:06,996 --> 00:46:09,461
Your dad was boasting all about it.

762
00:46:09,461 --> 00:46:11,819
He said you'll be the one to pay us back.

763
00:46:12,740 --> 00:46:14,137
So?

764
00:46:16,039 --> 00:46:18,493
How will you repay us?

765
00:46:18,493 --> 00:46:19,706
Why would I pay for his debt?

766
00:46:19,706 --> 00:46:23,193
Why? Because your dad
told us to collect from you!

767
00:46:25,162 --> 00:46:26,903
Okay?

768
00:46:26,903 --> 00:46:30,184
If you're so talented, surely you get
sponsorships and scholarships.

769
00:46:30,184 --> 00:46:31,878
So there's all that money.

770
00:46:31,878 --> 00:46:35,637
I wonder if you get bonuses
for winning tournaments?

771
00:46:37,485 --> 00:46:41,624
Then we'll have to support him so that
he can keep winning, isn't that right?

772
00:46:41,624 --> 00:46:44,142
Make sure no one else wins, you get me?

773
00:46:44,142 --> 00:46:45,427
Well, then, sir.

774
00:46:45,427 --> 00:46:48,471
Should we break the whole Judo team's legs?

775
00:46:50,786 --> 00:46:52,757
- Shut up.
- What did you say, you little mongrel?

776
00:46:52,757 --> 00:46:54,905
Oh, look who's mad.

777
00:46:56,387 --> 00:46:58,405
Don't lay a finger on our judo team.

778
00:46:59,590 --> 00:47:01,973
So you really cherish your team, huh?

779
00:47:02,917 --> 00:47:03,965
Little boy.

780
00:47:03,965 --> 00:47:06,825
I guess you're too young to understand this,

781
00:47:06,825 --> 00:47:10,236
but you just told me your greatest weakness.

782
00:47:10,236 --> 00:47:11,464
Get it now?

783
00:47:12,272 --> 00:47:13,499
- How dare you!
- Back down.

784
00:47:13,499 --> 00:47:14,770
Hey, hey, hey. Calm down.

785
00:47:14,770 --> 00:47:16,686
Oh, you silly boy.

786
00:47:16,686 --> 00:47:18,664
You're just full of surprises, aren't you?

787
00:47:22,023 --> 00:47:23,920
Get a load of this guy!

788
00:47:27,922 --> 00:47:30,740
Oh, just wait and see. Stop copying my move!

789
00:47:30,740 --> 00:47:32,538
You little...

790
00:47:36,821 --> 00:47:38,085
Oh, this guy's funny.

791
00:47:38,085 --> 00:47:40,067
- Hey, hey. Loosen up.
- Let him go.

792
00:47:40,067 --> 00:47:42,203
- He's falling a bit short.
- Let go.

793
00:47:42,926 --> 00:47:44,241
Oh, god damn it!

794
00:47:44,241 --> 00:47:47,024
- What are you guys standing around for?
- I said let go!

795
00:47:49,911 --> 00:47:51,729
- Scared me there for a second.
- You little bastard!

796
00:47:51,729 --> 00:47:54,626
- Stay down!
- Let me at him, too!

797
00:47:54,626 --> 00:47:57,798
- I'll kill you! Die! Die!
- Stop blocking!

798
00:47:59,230 --> 00:48:01,088
Hey, guys.

799
00:48:01,088 --> 00:48:03,039
- Let him stand.
- Yes, sir.

800
00:48:04,692 --> 00:48:06,758
- Get up, bastard.
- Stand up.

801
00:48:09,042 --> 00:48:11,000
You're dead now, little rat.

802
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:13,483
Hold him there. Hold tight.

803
00:48:13,483 --> 00:48:15,183
You bastard...

804
00:48:18,499 --> 00:48:19,757
Sir!

805
00:48:20,982 --> 00:48:23,012
- What the...
- Who the hell are you?

806
00:48:33,776 --> 00:48:35,823
How dare you!

807
00:48:51,073 --> 00:48:52,773
Hey! Are you alright?

808
00:48:55,210 --> 00:48:56,524
Why are you here?

809
00:48:56,524 --> 00:48:58,959
It doesn't matter. Who are these people?

810
00:49:01,318 --> 00:49:04,143
Hey, you two. Mr. Skinny and Mr. Bald.

811
00:49:04,143 --> 00:49:05,819
Just who are you guys?

812
00:49:05,819 --> 00:49:08,534
I'm not Mr. Bald.
I'm Real Love Capital's Department Manager!

813
00:49:08,534 --> 00:49:11,877
I'm not Mr. Skinny.
I'm the Team Leader of Real Love Capital!

814
00:49:11,877 --> 00:49:14,297
Capital? Real Love?

815
00:49:14,297 --> 00:49:16,688
Wow, that's an awful name.

816
00:49:16,688 --> 00:49:19,321
I'll take skinny,
you take the bald one. Got it?

817
00:49:19,321 --> 00:49:21,573
- Okay.
- Come here, you!

818
00:49:21,573 --> 00:49:23,584
Ow, owie... blood...

819
00:49:23,584 --> 00:49:26,080
- I'm bleeding!
- Sir?

820
00:49:26,080 --> 00:49:28,007
Blood! I'm bleeding!

821
00:49:29,597 --> 00:49:31,368
I'm bleeding out! It's all sticky!

822
00:49:31,368 --> 00:49:32,536
Blood?

823
00:49:34,592 --> 00:49:36,100
This is sweat, sir!

824
00:49:36,100 --> 00:49:37,474
Sweat?

825
00:49:37,474 --> 00:49:38,575
Hey!

826
00:49:38,575 --> 00:49:39,914
- Hey!
- But it hurts!

827
00:49:39,914 --> 00:49:41,292
It's sweat, sir!

828
00:49:41,292 --> 00:49:43,469
I think my skull's fractured!

829
00:49:43,469 --> 00:49:44,610
They're running away!

830
00:49:44,610 --> 00:49:47,480
Ugh, Mommy... Mo-om!

831
00:49:47,480 --> 00:49:48,846
I have an ouchie...

832
00:49:53,981 --> 00:49:56,219
I'm about to lose it.

833
00:49:57,114 --> 00:49:59,820
Where are you, Jung Woo Jae?

834
00:50:06,012 --> 00:50:07,454
Did you find him?

835
00:50:07,454 --> 00:50:08,900
<i>Yeah.</i>

836
00:50:08,900 --> 00:50:12,589
<i>He's with me right now,
so you go on and head back to the dormitory.</i>

837
00:50:13,464 --> 00:50:15,685
- Okay.
- Bye.

838
00:50:51,806 --> 00:50:53,907
This is the worst.

839
00:50:55,308 --> 00:50:56,746
What is?

840
00:50:56,746 --> 00:50:58,773
I really...

841
00:50:58,773 --> 00:51:01,268
didn't want you to see this.

842
00:51:01,268 --> 00:51:03,852
What are you talking about, you bastard?
What does it matter?

843
00:51:03,852 --> 00:51:06,118
- Bastard?
- Are you...

844
00:51:06,761 --> 00:51:08,443
Are you embarrassed?

845
00:51:08,443 --> 00:51:11,406
Okay. Let me tell you something.

846
00:51:11,406 --> 00:51:12,515
Get this. Actually...

847
00:51:12,515 --> 00:51:15,063
I peed my pants in 2nd grade.

848
00:51:15,063 --> 00:51:16,227
Okay.

849
00:51:16,883 --> 00:51:18,018
What?

850
00:51:18,018 --> 00:51:19,446
It was sports day.

851
00:51:19,446 --> 00:51:21,338
The waiting line for the restroom was so long.

852
00:51:21,338 --> 00:51:23,971
I waited and waited,
but it just wasn't getting any shorter.

853
00:51:25,106 --> 00:51:28,027
It's a secret, okay? Nobody knows this.

854
00:51:28,027 --> 00:51:30,578
Yeah, of course I'll keep it a secret.

855
00:51:30,578 --> 00:51:32,393
So we're even?

856
00:51:32,393 --> 00:51:34,131
Or is this not enough?
You want to know something worse?

857
00:51:34,131 --> 00:51:35,343
No, no.

858
00:51:35,343 --> 00:51:37,043
I think I'm good.

859
00:51:47,730 --> 00:51:49,430
If I'm being honest...

860
00:51:50,273 --> 00:51:52,536
My dad is a real piece of work.

861
00:51:55,017 --> 00:51:57,981
I thought it all ended when I moved here,

862
00:52:01,395 --> 00:52:03,195
but I guess I can't really run from it.

863
00:52:13,338 --> 00:52:15,122
Oh, I'm sorry.

864
00:52:15,122 --> 00:52:16,866
I didn't mean to vent.

865
00:52:16,866 --> 00:52:19,223
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

866
00:52:20,690 --> 00:52:22,390
Thank you.

867
00:52:23,373 --> 00:52:25,073
Thanks for telling me.

868
00:52:27,870 --> 00:52:32,888
This is the perfect time for some soju.

869
00:52:32,888 --> 00:52:33,912
Ha Na, you...

870
00:52:33,912 --> 00:52:35,612
Do you drink?

871
00:52:37,278 --> 00:52:38,662
No, dummy.

872
00:52:38,662 --> 00:52:41,035
What I mean is, we should have
a drink together once we turn 20.

873
00:52:41,035 --> 00:52:42,745
- Oh, okay.
- Dummy!

874
00:52:42,745 --> 00:52:44,667
- Let's go!
- Okay.

875
00:52:58,035 --> 00:52:59,318
Go inside.

876
00:52:59,318 --> 00:53:01,022
Your parents must be worried.

877
00:53:01,022 --> 00:53:02,778
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

878
00:53:02,778 --> 00:53:04,478
Spend the night with me in my room.

879
00:53:05,075 --> 00:53:08,232
What? S-spend the night?

880
00:53:08,232 --> 00:53:09,979
- With you?
- Yeah.

881
00:53:11,302 --> 00:53:12,530
But...

882
00:53:12,530 --> 00:53:14,111
Your parents are home.

883
00:53:14,111 --> 00:53:16,336
I can't possibly stay the night
in your room, Ha Na.

884
00:53:18,000 --> 00:53:19,762
Oh, no, I meant Ha Ru's room.

885
00:53:19,762 --> 00:53:21,712
Spend the night over in Yoon Ha Ru's room.

886
00:53:21,712 --> 00:53:24,505
They won't let you in the dorm now, so...

887
00:53:25,109 --> 00:53:26,981
- Yeah, you're right.
- Yeah.

888
00:53:26,981 --> 00:53:28,092
Let's head in.

889
00:53:28,092 --> 00:53:29,430
Okay.

890
00:53:34,717 --> 00:53:37,577
<i>What was I even thinking?</i>

891
00:53:37,577 --> 00:53:39,070
<i>Get it together!</i>

892
00:54:44,823 --> 00:54:47,461
I want soboro bread...

893
00:54:47,461 --> 00:54:48,942
Get me some soboro bread...

894
00:54:48,942 --> 00:54:50,708
<i>Jung Woo Jae slept over at our place.</i>

895
00:54:50,708 --> 00:54:52,377
<i>He was gone when I woke up.</i>

896
00:54:52,377 --> 00:54:54,737
<i>Is he at the dormitory?</i>

897
00:54:59,405 --> 00:55:00,760
Yes?

898
00:55:01,475 --> 00:55:03,175
Good morning, sir.

899
00:55:04,796 --> 00:55:06,414
This is Woo Jae's locker, right?

900
00:55:06,414 --> 00:55:07,890
Yes, sir.

901
00:55:07,890 --> 00:55:09,689
What's going on?

902
00:55:09,689 --> 00:55:12,269
Wait, what are you doing? That's his stuff.

903
00:55:13,738 --> 00:55:16,547
He withdrew the deposit
for the dormitory and is moving out.

904
00:55:16,547 --> 00:55:18,011
He's quitting judo.

905
00:55:18,011 --> 00:55:19,711
Wait, what?

906
00:55:20,397 --> 00:55:23,168
Why won't you answer, Jung Woo Jae?

907
00:55:24,239 --> 00:55:27,199
What could possibly have happened?

908
00:55:34,355 --> 00:55:36,631
Hey, four bowls for breakfast is too much!

909
00:55:40,922 --> 00:55:41,936
What?

910
00:55:41,936 --> 00:55:43,636
Where's all the stuff gone?

911
00:55:44,975 --> 00:55:46,675
Did he leave?

912
00:55:47,484 --> 00:55:48,979
I don't know.

913
00:55:52,280 --> 00:55:54,263
What's this camcorder doing here?

914
00:55:56,194 --> 00:55:57,734
[Yoon Ha Na]

915
00:56:03,579 --> 00:56:05,279
Out of battery...

916
00:56:07,795 --> 00:56:09,592
Hey, turn the air conditioning on.

917
00:56:09,592 --> 00:56:11,093
How does that sound?

918
00:56:11,924 --> 00:56:14,713
Yoon Ha Ru, answer the phone!

919
00:56:36,730 --> 00:56:40,064
[Yoon Ha Na]

920
00:56:45,321 --> 00:56:46,747
<i>What?</i>

921
00:56:46,747 --> 00:56:49,648
<i>I'm back home... all of a sudden?</i>

922
00:56:56,497 --> 00:56:58,612
[May 25th, Monday]
<i>The award ceremony...</i>

923
00:56:58,612 --> 00:57:00,312
<i>is tomorrow?</i>

924
00:57:01,819 --> 00:57:02,884
[Woo Jae]

925
00:57:02,909 --> 00:57:03,590
[No results]

926
00:57:16,010 --> 00:57:19,497
<i>The number you have reached is not in service.</i>

927
00:57:27,942 --> 00:57:29,642
<i>- What?</i>
- Yes.

928
00:57:30,359 --> 00:57:33,909
- What? They're releasing an article?
<i>- Boss?</i>

929
00:57:33,909 --> 00:57:37,591
On the day before the award ceremony?
Those snakes.

930
00:57:37,591 --> 00:57:39,755
Ha Na's schedule will go as we planned.

931
00:57:39,755 --> 00:57:41,868
<i>I'm... me.</i>

932
00:57:41,868 --> 00:57:42,893
<i>I'm back.</i>

933
00:57:42,893 --> 00:57:44,135
As soon as the revised complaint is ready,

934
00:57:44,135 --> 00:57:46,429
I don't care if it's in the
middle of the night, just email me.

935
00:57:46,429 --> 00:57:48,240
Don't forget to CC me.

936
00:57:48,240 --> 00:57:49,264
Good.

937
00:57:49,288 --> 00:57:50,566
[Yoon Ha Na]

938
00:57:52,540 --> 00:57:54,210
<i>Where are you?</i>

939
00:57:54,210 --> 00:57:57,180
I'm at the company. Ye Rang's office.

940
00:57:57,180 --> 00:57:58,583
<i>Get over here right now.</i>

941
00:57:58,583 --> 00:58:00,348
Huh? Where are you?

942
00:58:00,348 --> 00:58:03,802
The award ceremony is tomorrow.
Where would I be other than at home?

943
00:58:03,802 --> 00:58:05,293
Ah, right, okay!

944
00:58:05,293 --> 00:58:07,196
I'll be there in a second.

945
00:58:07,196 --> 00:58:10,289
You're leaving me in the middle of a date?

946
00:58:10,289 --> 00:58:13,000
Did I just hear that right?

947
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:16,077
Or did you seriously lose
all your common sense, Yoon Ha Ru?

948
00:58:18,322 --> 00:58:20,095
No, it's not that, I mean, it's...

949
00:58:20,095 --> 00:58:21,156
Well?

950
00:58:21,156 --> 00:58:25,102
Is there someone new
who's willing to take the lead?

951
00:58:25,102 --> 00:58:27,299
No, I swear it's nothing like that.

952
00:58:27,299 --> 00:58:30,059
But, yeah, she does take the lead, I guess.

953
00:58:31,978 --> 00:58:36,739
How am I supposed to take this, Yoon Ha Ru?

954
00:58:36,739 --> 00:58:38,439
Lovingly?

955
00:58:40,594 --> 00:58:42,294
I mean...

956
00:58:42,945 --> 00:58:44,360
It's just Ha Na.

957
00:58:44,360 --> 00:58:45,393
Huh?

958
00:58:45,393 --> 00:58:47,896
What's up with Ha Na?
Do you want me to come with?

959
00:58:47,896 --> 00:58:49,297
I'll call you when I get there!

960
00:58:49,297 --> 00:58:50,997
Love you!

961
00:58:52,328 --> 00:58:54,840
[Woo Jae is missing in both the past
and the present. What went wrong?]

962
00:58:54,840 --> 00:58:56,241
No, no.

963
00:58:56,241 --> 00:58:58,194
My friend, Woo Jae.

964
00:58:58,194 --> 00:58:59,697
[Water triggers it? Not just the Ha Na and Ha Ru,
but the camcorder needs to be wet, too]

965
00:58:59,697 --> 00:59:00,908
[How does the camcorder choose the
specific time to travel to? Is it random?]

966
00:59:01,295 --> 00:59:03,628
What do you mean, you don't know him?

967
00:59:05,136 --> 00:59:07,888
Darling, did you have too much wine?

968
00:59:07,888 --> 00:59:11,100
<i>I checked the whole list
of employees at the security agency.</i>

969
00:59:11,100 --> 00:59:12,959
<i>But I found nobody with the name Jung Woo Jae.</i>

970
00:59:12,959 --> 00:59:15,928
Alright, then. I'll call you back later.

971
00:59:15,928 --> 00:59:17,713
<i>Okay.</i>

972
00:59:17,713 --> 00:59:19,830
She says she doesn't know Woo Jae.

973
00:59:19,830 --> 00:59:22,547
Just how much did we change this time?

974
00:59:26,702 --> 00:59:29,206
Will this actually help us find the pattern?

975
00:59:29,206 --> 00:59:31,346
Are you sure about it?

976
00:59:31,346 --> 00:59:33,858
You and I, together, with the camcorder,
fall into a body of water.

977
00:59:33,858 --> 00:59:35,452
That's what triggers the time travel.

978
00:59:35,452 --> 00:59:37,168
And the time we travel to...

979
00:59:37,168 --> 00:59:39,938
is based on the videos
kept in the camcorder's memory.

980
00:59:39,938 --> 00:59:42,135
But as for the rules...

981
00:59:42,135 --> 00:59:43,718
I don't know.

982
00:59:47,516 --> 00:59:50,557
Maybe the camcorder decides?

983
00:59:50,557 --> 00:59:51,982
What?

984
00:59:53,540 --> 00:59:54,771
Think about it.

985
00:59:54,771 --> 00:59:58,677
Maybe there is no other rule,
except for the diving part.

986
00:59:58,677 --> 01:00:00,804
Maybe it's just on the camcorder's whims...

987
01:00:00,804 --> 01:00:02,768
So it's randomized, maybe?

988
01:00:02,768 --> 01:00:05,526
Well, I can't say you're absolutely wrong.

989
01:00:05,526 --> 01:00:08,600
I like it when things are simple.

990
01:00:08,600 --> 01:00:10,898
This camcorder is giving me a headache.

991
01:00:13,185 --> 01:00:15,206
The award ceremony is tomorrow.

992
01:00:15,206 --> 01:00:17,036
Yeah, it is.

993
01:00:17,036 --> 01:00:18,609
He... will be there.

994
01:00:18,609 --> 01:00:20,309
The ceremony...

995
01:00:22,941 --> 01:00:24,592
The ceremony...

996
01:00:24,592 --> 01:00:26,039
Are you going?

997
01:00:26,927 --> 01:00:28,581
- I have to.
- Don't even think about it!

998
01:00:28,581 --> 01:00:30,116
What if he really does show up?

999
01:00:30,116 --> 01:00:32,582
It's fine because we know he'll be there.

1000
01:00:32,582 --> 01:00:34,282
That way, I can avoid him.

1001
01:00:35,033 --> 01:00:36,733
Or maybe even catch him.

1002
01:00:37,847 --> 01:00:39,930
No, you can't. It's too dangerous.

1003
01:00:39,930 --> 01:00:41,801
I know.

1004
01:00:41,801 --> 01:00:44,344
I'm sure Woo Jae's alive somewhere.

1005
01:00:44,344 --> 01:00:47,533
Let's get that bastard tomorrow
and go find Woo Jae.

1006
01:00:53,607 --> 01:00:55,366
Then...

1007
01:00:55,366 --> 01:00:57,154
Just promise me one thing.

1008
01:00:57,820 --> 01:00:59,495
Tomorrow, at the ceremony,

1009
01:00:59,495 --> 01:01:01,407
whatever happens there...

1010
01:01:02,082 --> 01:01:04,298
promise me you'll put yourself first.

1011
01:01:04,298 --> 01:01:07,883
To me, what matters the most tomorrow
is saving you.

1012
01:01:07,883 --> 01:01:09,812
You'll have to be alive to find Woo Jae.

1013
01:01:10,446 --> 01:01:11,962
Understood?

1014
01:01:13,772 --> 01:01:15,150
Yes.

1015
01:01:38,559 --> 01:01:40,701
[Baekryong Film Awards]

1016
01:01:48,282 --> 01:01:52,057
[Congratulations on the award,
Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1017
01:01:52,057 --> 01:01:53,757
Have a nice day.

1018
01:01:58,756 --> 01:02:00,163
<i>Right now,</i>

1019
01:02:00,163 --> 01:02:01,678
<i>the clock reads half past six.</i>

1020
01:02:01,678 --> 01:02:02,844
<i>The award goes to...</i>

1021
01:02:02,844 --> 01:02:05,877
<i>Yoon Ha Na, from "I Was There in Your Night."</i>

1022
01:02:05,877 --> 01:02:07,222
<i>Congratulations.</i>

1023
01:02:07,222 --> 01:02:11,103
<i>The ceremony ends at 11.</i>

1024
01:02:14,152 --> 01:02:16,282
<i>Everyone's leaving. Let's go.</i>

1025
01:02:16,282 --> 01:02:19,408
<i>The time frame in which Woo Jae and I
were together in the waiting room...</i>

1026
01:02:19,408 --> 01:02:21,108
<i>Hey, Jung Woo Jae.</i>

1027
01:02:21,805 --> 01:02:25,285
[Seok Min]
<i>is roughly between 11:30 and 11:40.</i>

1028
01:02:28,095 --> 01:02:29,838
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

1029
01:02:29,838 --> 01:02:31,538
He's so handsome!

1030
01:02:40,325 --> 01:02:42,356
<i>Five hours from now...</i>

1031
01:02:43,248 --> 01:02:45,272
<i>Someone...</i>

1032
01:02:45,272 --> 01:02:47,821
<i>will be pointing a knife at me.</i>

1033
01:02:56,200 --> 01:02:58,037
<i>Thank goodness...</i>

1034
01:02:58,037 --> 01:03:00,367
<i>You're not here to protect me this time,</i>

1035
01:03:05,226 --> 01:03:07,602
<i>but I've returned to this moment.</i>

1036
01:03:28,767 --> 01:03:30,314
<i>Don't be scared.</i>

1037
01:03:30,314 --> 01:03:32,352
<i>Just be yourself.</i>

1038
01:03:32,352 --> 01:03:35,156
<i>You're not here to keep me safe today.</i>

1039
01:03:35,156 --> 01:03:36,622
<i>But I...</i>

1040
01:04:08,685 --> 01:04:10,692
<i>I will survive, no matter what...</i>

1041
01:04:12,058 --> 01:04:15,188
[Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1042
01:04:40,528 --> 01:04:44,437
[Congratulations on the award,
Actress Yoon Ha Na]

1043
01:04:57,905 --> 01:04:59,572
<i>And I will save you.</i>

1044
01:04:59,572 --> 01:05:01,272
<i>Jung Woo Jae.</i>

1045
01:05:21,756 --> 01:05:24,557
[Dive Into You]

1046
01:05:25,077 --> 01:05:26,468
<i>What is this?</i>

1047
01:05:26,468 --> 01:05:28,284
<i>The scar on his arm.</i>

1048
01:05:28,284 --> 01:05:29,534
<i>I know I saw it.</i>

1049
01:05:29,534 --> 01:05:30,591
<i>Let's go back again.</i>

1050
01:05:30,591 --> 01:05:31,937
<i>We can find him.</i>

1051
01:05:34,284 --> 01:05:36,368
<i>How much does he owe in total?</i>

1052
01:05:36,368 --> 01:05:38,419
<i>You said you'd pay me back for today.</i>

1053
01:05:38,419 --> 01:05:40,645
<i>Korea's national team judo player,
Jung Woo Jae!</i>

1054
01:05:40,645 --> 01:05:42,367
<i>Win the gold.</i>

1055
01:05:42,367 --> 01:05:43,688
<i>Something's off.</i>

1056
01:05:45,662 --> 01:05:47,552
<i>Something's really off.</i>

1057
01:05:47,552 --> 01:05:48,326
<i>Yoon Ha Na?</i>

1058
01:05:48,326 --> 01:05:50,370
<i>Jung Woo Jae, get up.</i>

1059
01:05:50,370 --> 01:05:53,243
<i>You saw the way he looked at me, right?</i>

1060
01:05:53,243 --> 01:05:56,063
<i>It was so intense, I thought I'd melt!</i>
